## 1. Brief Introduction and Problem Definition

Plant Pal is an IoT-based smart plant care system. It uses environmental sensors to collect real-time data and leverages AI to analyze the plant's growing conditions, then delivers care advice to the user through scheduled reports and voice interaction.

We've all been there — you buy a plant, put it by the window, water it every now and then, and hope for the best. But the truth is, most of us have no idea whether the environment is actually good for the plant. Is it getting enough light? Is the soil too dry? Too wet? Plants don't show signs of stress until it's already too late, and by then you're left wondering what went wrong.

That's exactly the problem Plant Pal sets out to solve. Instead of guessing, you get a system that watches the environment for you and tells you, in plain language, what your plant needs right now.

---

## 2. Motivation

This project started from what we learned in Lab 3, where we built a basic IoT sensor node with Arduino and MQTT. That got us thinking — we can already collect environmental data, but just showing numbers on a screen isn't very useful to a real user. At the same time, AI is everywhere right now, especially large language models that can understand context and have natural conversations. So the idea was pretty straightforward: what if we bring the two together? Let the IoT side handle the sensing, and let AI handle the thinking and the interaction with the user. That combination is what makes Plant Pal more than just a sensor board — it becomes something you can actually talk to and get real advice from.

---

## 3. Achievable Objectives

- Integrate DHT11, HW-390 soil moisture, and light sensors on an Arduino node.
- Publish sensor readings via MQTT every 30 minutes.
- Deploy OpenClaw cloud agent for automated plant health analysis.
- Push scheduled care reports to Feishu every 6 hours via cron tasks.
- Enable voice queries and camera analysis through xiaozhi ESP32.
- Establish MCP-based communication between xiaozhi and OpenClaw.


